{"ts":"2026-08-07T06:28:26.696Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"077176c9c9193448b4c63511","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"1","source":"environment"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.224","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-u1baah"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A commit pushed directly to the default branch can never be released: both analyzer-evidence fallbacks presuppose a pull request, and nothing declares that precondition"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The hosted analysis gate requires a DeepScan commit status and a CodeFactor check run on the exact release candidate, and both analyzers are configured to run on pull-request branches only. On this repository a pull-request head carries DeepScan success as a commit status and CodeFactor success as a check run, while the squash commit that lands on the default branch carries neither. The gate bridges that with two fallbacks: an identical-tree merge parent, and the head of the single pull request whose tree matches the candidate. Both fallbacks presuppose that the candidate arrived through a pull request.\n\nA commit pushed directly to the default branch satisfies neither. It has no second parent, so the merge-parent path exits immediately, and it has no associated pull request, so the squash-head lookup returns nothing. The gate then reports that the DeepScan status is missing for the exact commit, which names the absent external artifact rather than the absent workflow that would have produced it, and gives no indication that arriving through a pull request is a precondition of releasing at all.\n\nThe consequence is that a direct push to the default branch does not merely fail one cut; it blocks every subsequent scheduled cut until a pull-request-merged commit lands, because the candidate is always the current head. Observed 2026-08-07: every repository-owned check passed on the candidate, twenty-four in total including all four coverage shards and the exact-coverage gate at 100 percent, the artifact for the next version was built, and the pipeline stopped on the absent external status.\n\nNothing declares this precondition. The contributing guidance describes branching for pull requests as a convention, the gate help says only that the exact head must already be pushed so that analyzer results exist, and no gate, validation check or health check reports that the current head can never be released. The precondition is real, load-bearing, and discoverable only by attempting a release."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":1},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:ci","gate","release","ux"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-07T06:28:26.696Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-07T06:28:26.696Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":240},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"The release pipeline reports, before it builds anything, whether the current head can satisfy the analyzer evidence requirement, and names the workflow rather than the missing external artifact when it cannot; A commit that reached the default branch without a pull request either has a declared path to analyzer evidence or is refused with that reason stated, and the choice is recorded as a decision; The precondition that a releasable commit arrives through a pull request is declared wherever the release contract is declared, not left to be discovered by a failed cut; A negative control proves an unanalyzed commit still cannot release, so declaring the precondition never becomes a way to skip the analyzers"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-u9d0"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-23lmm5","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-07T06:28:26.696Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-39cqqx","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-08-07T06:28:26.696Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-e02lgu","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-08-07T06:28:26.696Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-xp1xsw","kind":"implements","created_at":"2026-08-07T06:28:26.696Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"7c3f0ab985aef75079b7b860a0d9c70fa311dc7c44f9055d778115d4ab044f62","message":""}
{"ts":"2026-08-11T13:52:31.175Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"e3bd70efeed1d617d5fc3f49","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"max","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"planner","source":"inferred","confidence":"high","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["focus:pm-doxj","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-doxj","source":"inferred","confidence":"high","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["focus:pm-doxj","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.227","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-11T13:52:31.175Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-08-11T13:52:31.175Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Reproduced in production on 2026-08-11, and it blocked the scheduled daily cut.\n\nSequence, all times UTC:\n\n- 04:02:48 the scheduled Auto Release run 31457243436 checked out main. HEAD was 3791ff12f74ff3f09c6062adca92ab8848d57ba7, a single-parent commit with no associated pull request.\n- 04:02:52 pull request 972 merged as 39d60f244779e8c4a451948988a0facbc48df824, four seconds after the checkout.\n- 04:09:37 hosted-analysis-gate refused with reason \"DeepScan status is missing for the exact commit\". The candidate carried exactly one commit status, codecov/patch, and no DeepScan or CodeFactor check run. Both fallbacks were unavailable: no second parent, and no pull request whose tree matched.\n- 04:09:38 blocker issue 973 opened. RECORDED_FAILURE_STAGE was hosted-analysis-gate, so the pm-x63izf fix reported the gate's own verdict rather than the preflight guess.\n- 04:12:23 blocker 973 closed, retry run 31457749989 started, checked out 39d60f24, and the same gate passed through the matching-pull-request fallback.\n- 04:21:18 v2026.8.11 tagged. npm shows 2026.8.11 as latest, and all three npx and bunx dispatch forms run it.\n\nSo the release succeeded only because the candidate changed between the two attempts. Nothing about 3791ff12 became releasable, and nothing ever will.\n\nPopulation measured the same day against the commits API rather than a subject-line heuristic: of the 103 commits on main since 2026-08-04, 37 have no associated pull request. That is 36 percent. main's HEAD at the time of measurement, 250b4030b4d246bdb6cb5f3ffb1fd1949be013c5, is one of them, so the default branch was sitting in an unreleasable state in the middle of an ordinary working day with no surface reporting it.\n\nThat last point is the half this item's acceptance criteria did not yet cover. AC1 requires the release pipeline to report releasability before it builds, which is a check inside a release attempt. Between attempts there is a window of up to 24 hours in which main is unreleasable and the only thing that will ever say so is tomorrow's 04:02 run. A new criterion has been added for that.\n"}]}],"before_hash":"7c3f0ab985aef75079b7b860a0d9c70fa311dc7c44f9055d778115d4ab044f62","after_hash":"386c0ea9fd549c89301eb1fac2cb450a101bccd07112ee9af41a68dca7073cbe"}
